      "skos:note": "To&nbsp;identify&nbsp;the respective&nbsp;antiretroviral drugs affected by the mutations&nbsp;present in this viral clone, use e.g. the&nbsp;„mutations list analysis“ function of the&nbsp;public HIV-Grade site&nbsp;at:www.hiv-grade.de/grade_new/",
      "EVORAO:preparationTechnique": "solid phase column extraction",
      "EVORAO:observedMutations": "mutations as indicated in the name; backbone is NL-BX:\r\nThe virus genome is derived from pNL-NF (pNL4-3 with shortened cellular flank) (doi.org/10.1016/j.jcv.2006.05.001), after introduction of a unique BamHI site 5’ (ggagcc2207ggaTcc; A->S in Pol; E->D in Gag) and an XmaI site 3’ (ccagga2589ccCggG; silent in Env; L->S in Rev) from the protease gene, respectively. The original BamHI site as position 8465 was removed (GGATCC->GGATCA change).\r\nClone carries a silent C2454T mutation in protease",
